  <prompt>
    Make the exported Word comments mirror the on-screen gutter. Today each w:comment bakes the RAW explanation prose +
    a hardcoded author. Build the export mirror: configurable AUTHOR (prop/config, not the literal at
    ComposeEditor.tsx:2146) · "Flagged clause" label (not "Grounded fact") · "Assessment says: …" · "Standard: …"
    (citation; full clause text when available). With 002's discrete fields there is NOTHING to string-parse — compose
    the structured export text from flaggedClause/assessment/standardRef. Server ApplyComment needs NO change.
  </prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Compose comment-thread export mapping, docx save flow.</role>
  <goal>A saved-then-opened-in-Word agreement shows structured comments identical in content to the gutter; author configurable.</goal>

  <context>
